Changes to be done before moving to Production :

1. Persist accounts and transfers in a transactional database. The in-memory repository loses state on restart and cannot perform transfers across application instances.
2. Add timeout and retry for lock (tryLock with defined timeout and retry count),  and request (request timeout, safe retries with backoff, backed by idempotency keys so a client retry after a timeout cannot move money twice.)
3. Make the debit and credit one atomic transaction, with database-level concurrency control.
4. Notification to be sent asynchronously via queue or Kafka to reduce latency and separate control of retry
5. Authentication and authorisation, so a sender can only move money out of accounts they own. Add rate limiting.
6. Structured logs with correlation ids (splunk) , metrics and request tracing (Grafana, Dynatrace) , Actuator health and readiness probes, alerting.
7.  Integration tests against a real database
8.  CI/CD pipeline with build, coverage, test run and vulnerability scanning
9. Add Containerised deployment config


